#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:439 includes/class-wpcpm-settings.php:494
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-mentors-dashboard.php:683
msgid "Currently mentoring"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:441
msgid ""
"One status per line. Students holding any of these appear under \"Currently "
"mentoring\" on their mentor's page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:446
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-mentors-dashboard.php:706
msgid "Past students"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:448
msgid ""
"Statuses that mean mentoring has finished. These students appear in a "
"separate, collapsed section. Leave empty to show only current students. A "
"status listed in both boxes counts as current."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:453
msgid "When a mentor is no longer active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:455
msgid "Remove the Mentor role and clear their student list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:457 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:504
msgid "Leave the role in place"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:458
msgid "The account itself is never deleted either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:463
msgid "Invitation emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:465
msgid "Email each new mentor a password-reset link as their account is created"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:466
msgid ""
"Off by default. A first sync creates around ninety accounts at once, so "
"leave this off unless you mean to email all of them. Invitations are queued "
"and sent a few at a time rather than all inside the sync, so a mail limit "
"cannot swallow half of them unnoticed. You can also invite people one at a "
"time from the Mentors and Students screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:471
msgid "Automatic sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:473
msgid "Read Airtable on a schedule"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:474
msgid ""
"Students every three hours, mentors once a day: the student rows carry what "
"people are shown on their cards, and the mentors run costs one WordPress.org "
"profile read per mentor. A run already in progress is left to finish rather "
"than restarted. Either can also be run by hand from the Students and Mentors "
"screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:479
msgid "Mentor landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:481
msgid "Use the Mentor Report Card page as the mentor dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:482
msgid ""
"Mentors go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, "
"and get a \"Mentor Report Card\" link in the toolbar. They keep access to "
"their own profile screen, and a mentor who followed a link to somewhere "
"specific still lands there instead. Administrators are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:485 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:516
msgid "The page is missing - re-activate the plugin to recreate it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:494
msgid "Students module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:495
msgid ""
"Uses the same status lists as the Mentors module above - a current student "
"is anyone a mentor is currently mentoring."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:500
msgid "When a student leaves the program"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:502
msgid "Remove the Student role, so they lose access to Student-level content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:505
msgid ""
"The account itself is never deleted either way, and their program details "
"are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:510
msgid "Student landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:512
msgid "Use the My Program page as the student dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:513
msgid ""
"Students go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, "
"and get a \"My Program\" link in the toolbar. Same exceptions as for "
"mentors: a requested destination wins, their own profile screen stays "
"reachable, and anyone who can write posts is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:530
msgid "Save settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:556
msgid "Institutions module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:557
msgid ""
"Institutions are the schools and universities whose students are on the "
"program. Each has its own dashboard, its own people, and one Collaboration "
"Agreement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:571
msgid "Applications from institutions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:573
msgid "Take applications through the form on this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:574
msgid ""
"A public page anybody can post to. Every submission is stored for a program "
"manager to read on the Institutions screen, and nothing is created until "
"somebody approves it. While this is off the page shows one sentence saying "
"applications are closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:576
msgid ""
"No privacy policy page is set, so the form shows nothing to the public "
"however this is switched. Publish one and choose it under Settings, Privacy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:580 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:610
msgid "The page is missing: re-activate the plugin to recreate it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:588
msgid "Enrolment lists from institutions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:590
msgid "Let an institution send a list of students to enrol"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:591
msgid ""
"Adds an \"Enrol students\" section to the Institution Dashboard, where a "
"school chooses the program and the term and then adds one student or sends a "
"CSV. The list is read and checked against the program records, and the "
"school sees what was understood before anything is created. While this is "
"off the section does not appear at all."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: checks per hour, 2: rows per day.
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:595
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Ceilings per institution: %1$s checks an hour and %2$s students a day. Files "
"are read and never stored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:604
msgid "Institution landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:606
msgid "Use the Institution Dashboard page as the institution dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:607
msgid ""
"Institution accounts go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin "
"Dashboard, and get an \"Institution Dashboard\" link in the toolbar. Same "
"exceptions as for mentors and students."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:615
msgid "Create accounts automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:617
msgid ""
"Let the nightly sync create the first account for a Confirmed institution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:618
msgid ""
"From the Contact Email Airtable holds, and only for a Confirmed institution "
"whose agreement is recorded and that has never had a member. An address that "
"already belongs to an account is left alone and named on the Institutions "
"screen. With this off, accounts are created only when somebody presses the "
"button there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:623
msgid "When an institution leaves the pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:625
msgid "Remove its people, so they lose access to its students"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:627
msgid "Leave their access in place"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:628
msgid ""
"When Airtable moves an institution out of the stages the program treats as "
"active. The accounts themselves are never deleted either way, and the "
"agreement and the roster are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:633
msgid "Agreement review"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:635
msgid "days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:636
msgid ""
"How long a signed agreement may wait before the queue marks it overdue and "
"the nightly digest names it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:641
msgid "Who reviews agreements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:643
msgid "one@example.org, two@example.org"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:644
msgid ""
"Addresses told when an agreement arrives and sent the overdue digest. Leave "
"it empty and every program manager is written to, which reaches technical "
"administrators as well; set it before the first real upload."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:649
msgid "The agreement wording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:651
msgid "https://docs.google.com/document/d/..."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:652
msgid ""
"The Google Doc the plugin's copy of the Collaboration Agreement was taken "
"from, used by the Check against the Doc button. Held on this site rather "
"than in the code, because the document is editable by anyone holding its "
"link and the plugin's source is public. Google addresses only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:677
msgid "Two-factor authentication"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:682
msgid ""
"Nobody is asked for a second factor, because the Two Factor plugin is not "
"active on this site. Install and activate it, and the roles ticked below "
"will be asked for a code as well as a password at their next sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:687
msgid ""
"An account in a ticked role is asked for a code as well as its password, "
"from its next sign-in, with nothing to set up first: the code is emailed. "
"Each person can then set up an authenticator app on their own profile "
"screen, which is quicker and does not depend on their email. Untick "
"everything to ask nobody."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:692
msgid "Roles that must use it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:700
msgid "Program managers (administrators)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:717
msgid ""
"Students are left off by default: a student account holds that student's own "
"work, there are hundreds of them, and there is nobody to unlock the ones who "
"change phone. They can still turn it on for themselves."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:723
msgid "Where it stands"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: role name, 2: accounts covered, 3: accounts in the role, 4: accounts using an app.
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:731
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s: %2$d of %3$d covered, %4$d using an authenticator app."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:743
msgid ""
"Counted now, on this screen. An account that is covered but has no app is "
"using emailed codes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:760 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:770
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:192
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:237
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:501
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:540
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:832
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook.php:63
msgid "Need help?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:763
msgid ""
"A question box for people on the program, answered from the WordPress "
"documentation. The AI provider below does the searching, so nothing is "
"stored on this site - and without a provider there is no answer at all. Each "
"question, and the pages found for it, go to that company."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:772
msgid "Switch it on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:773
msgid ""
"Off means the question box answers nobody, the header button disappears and "
"the page it lives on is unpublished. Nothing is deleted, so switching it "
"back on restores all of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:778
msgid "Where answers come from"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:779
msgid ""
"The provider searches wordpress.org, make.wordpress.org, learn.wordpress.org "
"and developer.wordpress.org itself. Nothing is copied to this site, so there "
"is nothing to configure and nothing to refresh - and equally, no answer at "
"all without a provider below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:797
msgid "Answer provider"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:799
msgid ""
"Leave as \"None\" to keep everything on this site. Choosing a provider sends "
"each question, and the extracts that match it, to that company."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:804
msgid "Provider API key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:806
msgid ""
"Stored in the database and never sent to the browser - leave blank to keep "
"the current key. Get one free at aistudio.google.com for the Gemini provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:812
msgid "Model"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:814
msgid ""
"Leave as gemini-flash-latest unless you have a reason not to. It is an alias "
"that always points at the current Gemini Flash, so it cannot be retired out "
"from under this site - which has already happened twice to specific version "
"numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:818
msgid "Mentors and program managers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:819
msgid "Students and institutions as well"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:820
msgid "Anybody logged in to this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:821
msgid "Program managers only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:837
msgid "Who can ask"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:839
msgid ""
"Never anybody logged out, whatever this says. The documentation describes "
"running the program rather than being on it, which is why students are not "
"included by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:844
msgid "Questions per person per hour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:846
msgid ""
"How many questions one person may have answered in an hour, so a free tier "
"cannot be spent in an afternoon. Past the limit they are asked to come back "
"shortly. 0 removes the limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:858
msgid "Mail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:869
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%s invitation is waiting to be sent. They go out a few at a time in the "
"background."
msgid_plural ""
"%s invitations are waiting to be sent. They go out a few at a time in the "
"background."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:882
msgid ""
"Ninety people is a bad audience for a first look at a template. Send "
"yourself the invitation as a student, a mentor or an institution would "
"receive it - the three say different things."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:886
msgid "Email me the student invitation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:887
msgid "Email me the mentor invitation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:888
msgid "Email me the institution invitation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:915
msgid "Recent mail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:920
msgid ""
"Nothing sent yet. Bookings, cancellations, reminders and invitations are all "
"recorded here once they are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:935
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%s of these was refused by whatever handles mail on this site. That is a "
"delivery problem to fix, not a program one."
msgid_plural ""
"%s of these were refused by whatever handles mail on this site. That is a "
"delivery problem to fix, not a program one."
